mirror_matrix
=============

Write a function:

    def mirror_matrix(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> list

Given a 2D matrix (list of lists of integers), return a new matrix where
EACH ROW IS REVERSED (a horizontal mirror).

Examples:
    mirror_matrix([[1,2,3],
                   [4,5,6],
                   [7,8,9]])
    -> [[3,2,1],
        [6,5,4],
        [9,8,7]]

    mirror_matrix([[1,2],[3,4]])   -> [[2,1],[4,3]]
    mirror_matrix([])              -> []
